  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients with the all-client views of client_updates, client_performance, drift_by_round, feature_summary and subgroup_outcomes (Sex, AgeGroup, Income). The strongest evidence points to two free riders, WA and NE. Each uploads near-zero updates in several rounds (1, 2, 8, 12, 14, 16) and normal updates otherwise. Both are flagged on min_norm_ratio, and their local performance looks normal. I also report CT with low confidence (0.4): its GenHlth p99 is above the scale maximum, with a noise-adjusted z of 6.1, which suggests a missing-value sentinel. I could not confirm it, and its onset is unknown. No evidence of poisoning, label noise, prevalence shift, drift, subgroup bias or explanation instability cleared the noise thresholds. Several other single-statistic leads were not reported: ND's GenHlth low tail and PhysHlth mean (z_noise about -3.3), WV's MentHlth p99 (z_noise -5.3), DC's DiffWalk drift (z 3.9), GU's CITL (z -3.9), and the small-cell subgroup O/E outliers. Each is either below the threshold or from a small client. The budget was fully spent after the per-client update checks, so these leads could not be confirmed."
